      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A passive approach can indeed mislead you. A common culprit that causes small holes without leaving visible signs is wind damage, especially if your greenhouse is experiencing strong gusts or irregular airflow. Another possibility is transplant shock or physical damage during handling, although this might be less likely in a greenhouse environment. Consider inspecting plants during the day and possibly using a gentle agitation method to dislodge any debris or concealed damage.",
