      "role": "user",
      "content": "wind damage doesn't really make sense since the greenhouse is controlled, and the holes are very specific shapes, not just shredded leaves. it's just so strange. it's like they're being targeted by something very small that knows how to stay out of sight. \n\ncould it be some kind of soil-based pest? like something that stays underground or in the mulch and only comes up at certain times? i'm starting to get a bit paranoid about something being hidden in the shadows of the greenhouse.",
