      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I can understand the paranoia. Soil-based pests are a possibility, although it's less common for them to cause such targeted damage. One possibility that comes to mind is a type of flea beetle or an ants colony that's not readily visible. Flea beetles can cause very small, irregular holes, and sometimes their larvae may feed on underground plant parts. Ants might also be hiding in mulch or soil, only emerging at night to feed on plant sap. However, ants would typically create larger, more noticeable damage patterns.",
